# Security Enforcement

**ZERO TOLERANCE: Apply to EVERY app.**

## Critical Security Rules

| Priority | Rule | Pattern |
|----------|------|---------|
| CRITICAL | Input validation | Allowlist operations, validate types, sanitize strings |
| HIGH | Safe logging | Never log secrets, tokens, full objects |
| MEDIUM | XSS prevention | Use `textContent`, sanitize before `innerHTML` |
| MEDIUM | Secret handling | Use iparams, never hardcode, mask in UI |

## Input Validation (CRITICAL)

**MUST validate ALL SMI input. Use allowlists.**

```javascript
// SAFE: Allowlist
const ALLOWED_OPS = ['status', 'list', 'health'];
if (!ALLOWED_OPS.includes(args.operation)) {
  return { error: 'Not allowed' };
}

// SAFE: Type validation
const id = parseInt(args.id, 10);
if (isNaN(id) || id < 0) return { error: 'Invalid ID' };

// SAFE: String sanitization
function sanitize(str) {
  return String(str).replace(/[<>"'&]/g, '');
}
```

**Checklist:**
- [ ] Validate types (string, number, boolean)
- [ ] Sanitize strings (remove special chars)
- [ ] Use allowlists for enums
- [ ] Reject malformed input
- [ ] Never trust client data

## Safe Logging (HIGH)

**Log only status and non-sensitive IDs.**

```javascript
// SAFE
console.log('App installed');
console.log('Ticket created:', args.data?.ticket?.id);
console.error('Operation failed:', e.message);

// UNSAFE - NEVER DO
console.log(args); // Full object
console.log(args.iparams.api_key); // Secret
console.log(args.oauth_token); // Token
```

**Checklist:**
- [ ] Never log full objects
- [ ] Never log tokens, keys, passwords
- [ ] Log only operation status + IDs
- [ ] Use `e.message` only for errors

## XSS Prevention (MEDIUM)

**Use `textContent` for data. Sanitize before `innerHTML`.**

```javascript
// SAFE
element.textContent = userData;
element.setAttribute('data-id', ticketId);

// UNSAFE
element.innerHTML = userData; // XSS risk
element.outerHTML = `<div>${data}</div>`; // XSS risk
```

**Sanitize if innerHTML required:**
```javascript
function sanitizeHTML(str) {
  const div = document.createElement('div');
  div.textContent = str;
  return div.innerHTML;
}
element.innerHTML = sanitizeHTML(userData);
```

## Secret Handling (MEDIUM)

**Use iparams. Never hardcode. Mask in UI.**

```javascript
// SAFE: iparams
const apiKey = args.iparams.api_key;

// SAFE: Masked display
const masked = '****' + apiKey.slice(-4);

// UNSAFE - NEVER DO
const apiKey = 'sk-1234567890'; // Hardcoded
console.log(apiKey); // Logged
```

**Checklist:**
- [ ] Use `config/iparams.json` for secrets
- [ ] Never hardcode keys/tokens
- [ ] Mask in UI (show last 4 chars)
- [ ] Never log secrets

## Quick Reference

| Security Need | Safe Pattern |
|---------------|--------------|
| Input validation | Allowlist + type check + sanitize |
| Logging | Status + IDs only, never secrets |
| DOM update | `textContent` or sanitized `innerHTML` |
| Secrets | iparams, masked display, never log |

